Saber is a persistent vertical panel for Wayland in the tradition of the Unity 7
launcher, built for the hikari-sakura compositor on FreeBSD. Down its column sit
an application menu button, pinned and running applications with their
window-count pips and focus arrow, the sheet indicator, mounted devices, the
trash, the system tray and the session controls.

It is a pure Wayland client. Windows are listed and acted on through
wlr-foreign-toplevel-management, surfaces are placed with wlr-layer-shell, and
the compositor's sheets are read over its own control socket. Nothing about the
compositor is patched or assumed beyond what it already publishes, and the panel
draws itself with cairo and pango rather than linking a widget toolkit.

Saber has no theme of its own: it reads the sixteen-colour palette out of the
user's hikari.conf, so retheming the compositor retints the panel along with the
top bar and the lock screen.

The system tray is a StatusNotifierItem host. Exactly one process on a session
bus may own that role, so Saber and "sofi -tray-daemon" cannot both run; build
without the TRAY option to keep the latter.

Saber is the panel layer of the Sakura desktop, alongside the sakura display
manager, the hikari-sakura compositor and the sofi launcher, and depends on none
of them at build time.
